the clark county school district updates  the transition plan to the hybrid  instructional model  80s now reporter kristen drummond has  the very latest on the guide  ccsd posted the now 235 page guide on  the website  slightly more reading material than the  original document released in november  but  it offers updated information about  school protocols cleaning operations and  the overall transition ccsd is preparing  to welcome back only pre-kindergarten to  third grade students in buildings on  march  1st all staff and students must wear a  face covering  but there are a few exceptions when it  can be removed  a few pages outline the type of personal  protective equipment or  ppe required for employees depending on  the job  the document also highlights teacher  assignments and either cohort a  b or c cohort c is full-time distance  education  and the other two incorporate in-person  and online learning  towards the end of the guide the  district offers sample schedules to see  what a typical day looks like for not  only elementary but middle school  and high schools the document offers  direction for secondary schools but  it remains unknown when hybrid learning  will start for those grade levels  the release of the updated guide comes  five days after lower elementary school  students had to choose between  continuing distance education or  starting hybrid learning  the timing frustrating some families who  wanted this information ahead of time  in the newsroom kristen drummond 8 news  now
 

